## agent-director's two sweeps as crontab lines: find-missing every 2 minutes,
## expire once a day. install.sh --schedule adds the lines below this block to
## the crontab of the user it runs as; the same lines are what its warning prints
## when no schedule is set up.
##
## Lines that start with two # are notes for you: install.sh does not install
## them. Every other line is installed, and every installed line carries the
## marker agent-director-schedule, which is how install.sh (a re-run) and
## uninstall.sh find and replace or remove exactly these lines and no others.
##
## To install them by hand, the easiest way is to copy the filled-in lines that
## install.sh's warning prints (they are these two lines with the placeholders
## filled). To fill them yourself, replace the two placeholders and add the
## lines to the crontab of the user the agents run as (crontab -e):
##   @@AGENT_DIRECTOR@@  the absolute path of the installed agent-director,
##                       ~/.config/agent-director/bin/agent-director, written out.
##   @@ENV_PREFIX@@      the environment cron does not give a job, as NAME=value
##                       words before the command. install.sh writes, always,
##                       PATH=<the directory of tmux>:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin
##                       (without the tmux directory and its colon when tmux is
##                       not on the PATH of the install); then, only when the
##                       agents' tmux server lives in a TMUX_TMPDIR,
##                       TMUX_TMPDIR=<that directory>; then, only when the
##                       install's $HOME is not the home directory of the user's
##                       passwd entry (cron sets HOME from that entry, and the
##                       binary keeps its files in $HOME/.config/agent-director),
##                       HOME=<the install's $HOME>. The value is never empty.
## Run as the agents' user, in the agents' tmux environment: find-missing run
## as another user, as root or against another tmux server can wrongly mark
## live rows missing, and expire can wrongly delete rows whose agent still
## runs. The config directory is $HOME/.config/agent-director, so the sweep
## needs the install's HOME (see HOME above). A % in a path is written \% in a
## crontab.
##
# agent-director-schedule: the find-missing and expire sweeps (install-agent-director skill, schedule/agent-director.cron)
*/2 * * * * @@ENV_PREFIX@@ @@AGENT_DIRECTOR@@ find-missing >/dev/null # agent-director-schedule
17 3 * * * @@ENV_PREFIX@@ @@AGENT_DIRECTOR@@ expire >/dev/null # agent-director-schedule
